#X obj 681 8 envelope;
#X obj 230 78 cnv 1 535 215 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -237178 -1 0;
#X text 240 83 Data type for a sound envelope. It contains points defined
by time and value. A point can have the stop property — this makes
the envelope stop at that point instead of continuing \, so multi-segment
envelopes can be created.;
#X text 240 168 A point also has a segment type property that defines
the following segment curve. It can be *step* \, *line* (default) or
*exp* (exponential).;
#X text 240 223 An exponential segment also has a curve property: 0
(linear) \, <0 (concave \, negatively curved) \, >0 (convex \, positively
curved).;
#X msg 50 341 ar 100 200 \, bang;
#X msg 232 341 exp 0 30 -2 1 100 -4 0 40 4 0.5 30 2 0 \, bang;
#X msg 69 370 adsr 10 30 60 150 \, bang;
#X msg 318 370 line 0.1 40 0.9 20 0.3 60 0 \, bang;
#X msg 88 399 ear 10 -2 60 -2 \, bang;
#X msg 318 399 sigmoid 0 40 14 1 100 8 0 \, bang;
#X msg 107 428 eadsr 20 -5 70 -12 30 100 -7 \, bang;
#X msg 462 428 sin2 0 80 1 80 0 \, bang;
